# Observed cross-stage evidence

| Design | Parents with placed descendants | Strict QoR ranking reversals | Pruning events |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| adder_32bit | 6 | 0 | 0 |
| multi_pipe_8bit | 6 | 0 | 0 |
| barrel_shifter | 6 | 0 | 0 |
| div_16bit | 6 | 0 | 2 |

The downstream categorical parameter domain is shared across parents. Upstream netlists change mapped cells/area and the physical geometry used by placement. This experiment does not demonstrate a change in which parameter values are legal. Timing feasibility is evaluated from actual placed slack, not inferred from structural similarity.

Strict reversals exclude ties. Different child coverage means this is an observed mechanism audit, not an oracle optimal-parent ranking. Early-prune loss is evaluated only when independent later observations exist and remains coverage-limited.
